WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:03.970
-Also, we are so excited
on this holiday week,

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:07.673
the final shows of 2023,
to have our dear friend

00:00:07.673 --> 00:00:10.276
and bandleader Fred Armisen
back with us on drums.

00:00:10.276 --> 00:00:14.414
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thanks.

00:00:14.414 --> 00:00:16.082
-Fred, once again,

00:00:16.082 --> 00:00:18.217
no one has accomplished more
in 2023 than you.

00:00:18.217 --> 00:00:20.252
You're always working. We're
happy when we have you here.

00:00:20.252 --> 00:00:22.821
We also know that you're out
on the road doing stand up,

00:00:22.821 --> 00:00:25.758
doing other projects,
and I'm always just blown away

00:00:25.758 --> 00:00:27.427
when I hear the things
you're working on.

00:00:27.427 --> 00:00:28.528
-Aww, thank you.

00:00:28.528 --> 00:00:30.429
-And I have to ask you,
is this true

00:00:30.429 --> 00:00:34.200
that you are releasing this week
your own Christmas album?

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.835
-I am.
-Wow.

00:00:35.835 --> 00:00:37.336
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you. Yeah.

00:00:37.336 --> 00:00:39.806
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:39.806 --> 00:00:42.575
It's a celebration
of the Mummy.

00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:44.343
You know, like...

00:00:44.343 --> 00:00:46.913
-The -- The horror movie
character of the Mummy?

00:00:46.913 --> 00:00:49.148
-Yeah. Well, people think of it
as a horror movie character,

00:00:49.148 --> 00:00:51.717
but it's just a character
for all seasons.

00:00:51.717 --> 00:00:53.986
So I'm just trying
to do something

00:00:53.986 --> 00:00:55.788
so, like, to include the Mummy

00:00:55.788 --> 00:00:58.491
in more Christmassy,
you know, things.

00:00:58.491 --> 00:01:00.960
And it's just like, you know --
-When you say, like, "more,"

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:02.462
like, I would say,
like, start --

00:01:02.462 --> 00:01:04.964
we're starting at zero, right?
[ Laughter ]

00:01:04.964 --> 00:01:07.266
Like, I feel like there are
zero holiday classics

00:01:07.266 --> 00:01:09.135
that include
the Mummy right now.

00:01:09.135 --> 00:01:10.236
-You're right about that...
-Yeah.

00:01:10.236 --> 00:01:11.538
-...actually.

00:01:11.538 --> 00:01:13.839
And this is just a way
to bring that back.

00:01:13.839 --> 00:01:15.675
Because Christmas --
-But, again, you say "back"...

00:01:15.675 --> 00:01:17.276
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.276 --> 00:01:19.545
Was there a time when there were
a lot of Mummy Christmas songs?

00:01:19.545 --> 00:01:21.614
-Just the old traditions,
you know what I mean?

00:01:21.614 --> 00:01:23.516
Like the old -- Like,
let's bring that back,

00:01:23.516 --> 00:01:25.718
like the 1800s
and, you know, like...

00:01:25.718 --> 00:01:28.221
-So in the 1800s, there were
a lot of Christmas songs

00:01:28.221 --> 00:01:29.889
that had the Mummy in them?
-I gather.

00:01:29.889 --> 00:01:32.458
[ Laughter ]

00:01:32.458 --> 00:01:35.094
-Did you do any research?
-Some. I --

00:01:35.094 --> 00:01:36.428
You know,
the way I do research

00:01:36.428 --> 00:01:37.630
is I've got a bunch of friends.

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:39.198
They are awesome.
I think they're here.

00:01:39.198 --> 00:01:41.300
You guys are great.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:43.236
You guys are here.

00:01:43.236 --> 00:01:45.171
-So it sounds -- It sounds like
maybe the whole audience.

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:46.339
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:46.339 --> 00:01:48.541
-It's most of them,
and they're the best.

00:01:48.541 --> 00:01:49.975
They're like --
But they're the best.

00:01:49.975 --> 00:01:52.512
They're -- They work so hard.
They're just so cool.

00:01:52.512 --> 00:01:54.380
They're down to earth,
they're sweet.

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:55.681
And they --
-I know you've been really

00:01:55.681 --> 00:01:57.082
keeping it under wraps, but...

00:01:57.082 --> 00:01:58.551
And you don't have to have
any music for it.

00:01:58.551 --> 00:02:00.753
Just, you know, a cappella,
could you just real quick

00:02:00.753 --> 00:02:02.354
sing us one of your Mummy
Christmas songs?

00:02:02.354 --> 00:02:04.157
-Oh, well, first of all,
it's just melodies.

00:02:04.157 --> 00:02:05.391
They're Mummy melodies.

00:02:05.391 --> 00:02:07.393
So there's no --
it's not the lyrics.

00:02:07.393 --> 00:02:10.363
It's just like...
[ Vocalizing ]

00:02:13.565 --> 00:02:14.634
-So, I'm sorry.

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:16.235
[ Laughter ]

00:02:16.235 --> 00:02:18.037
You're telling me --
I've seen the cover art.

00:02:18.037 --> 00:02:20.540
It's you with your arm around
a Mummy wearing a Santa hat.

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:22.408
-Yes.
-So I buy that...

00:02:22.408 --> 00:02:25.445
there's an expectation I'm going
to hear Mummy holiday songs,

00:02:25.445 --> 00:02:26.979
and it's all just melodies?

00:02:26.979 --> 00:02:28.681
-But you're going to picture
the mummies

00:02:28.681 --> 00:02:30.583
walking around at Christmas.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.583 --> 00:02:32.552
That's what you're
supposed to imagine.

00:02:33.753 --> 00:02:35.521
[ Laughter ]

00:02:35.521 --> 00:02:36.789
-How many songs are on it?

00:02:36.789 --> 00:02:38.057
-22.

00:02:38.057 --> 00:02:39.325
[ Laughter ]

00:02:39.325 --> 00:02:40.927
-Give it up for Fred Armisen,
everybody!

